Exactly.

This is actually where JNL becomes more valuable than a traditional wiki link system.

Instead of JD storing lots of paths, mirrors, summaries, and references, JD can store a very small amount of information and let JNL do the heavy lifting.


---

Optimized JD Model

A JD entry should primarily contain:

Name
Type
Authority
Definition
Purpose
JNL
Related JNLs
Tags
ReferenceMap

That's it.


---

